  "notes": "Format-support change with no new JavaScript API, so the inventory is the decode-support change itself, the markup negotiation surface (<picture>/<source type>), and the script detection pattern. Honest limits preserved on-page: BCD has no JPEG XL key at all (whole 8.1.5 dataset searched); ISO text is paywalled so format internals are linked (iso.org, jpegxl.info), not restated; the sources read record no Accept-header change, stated as such rather than claimed either way; no Edge version recorded; Firefox is Nightly-only per its own release notes even though the ChromeStatus vendor view reads 'Shipped/Shipping'. Detection snippets are gendn-derived, labelled, and mirror the probes the embedded showcase decode-probe demo runs against a real .jxl; an earlier draft's inline base64 'minimal JXL' was removed because its bytes could not be verified against any source. srcset and createImageBitmap appear only inside markup/script examples, not as members declared by the page's syntax block, so they carry no outOfScope entries (declared-surface rule); their pre-existing, unchanged nature is stated in the prose instead."
